  "query_preview": "..\nA fairly large upper low off the California coast will keep an \ninduced ridge to its east, allowing NE MT to experience dry \nconditions and warmer than normal temps through early Friday.\n\nBut the upper low will begin to merge with a western Canada \ntrough Friday. This will pull up Pacific moisture from the Desert\nSW while a surface low developing over southern MT pulls NE \ntracking showers across the western CWA through Saturday morning.\nThis will also allow NW winds to increase late Friday behind a \ncold front. The showers are expected to exit the CWA Saturday with\nsignificantly cooler high temps Saturday onward.\n\nRough conditions on Fort Peck Lake can be expected beginning\nFriday afternoon through Saturday afternoon. Check the forecast \nif you have plans to visit the area later this week.\n\nRainfall amounts looked to be greatest over central Montana and\nthe models have shifted the deterministic rain amounts west with\nthis run. Areas east of a Culbertson to Miles City line are not\nexpecting any QPF.\n\nBeyond Saturday, temps look to remain below normal as an upper\nridge early next week doesn't nudge east of the Pac NW.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nDid blend wind gusts late Friday with NBM90, otherwise thought\nwhat NBM gave me looked good.\n\nTFJ",
